! A local label character "Z" before any proof step.  Every "Z" appends a
! label map entry, and one with no step to name used to store -999, which
! is not a legal local label reference, so verifyProof() aborted with
! bug(2101) once a later label resolved to it.
!
! PROVE is the command that reaches it: VERIFY PROOF stops at the severe
! error, but PROVE runs verifyProof() over the proof string anyway.
verify proof *
prove z1
show new_proof /unknown
exit
prove z2
show new_proof /unknown
exit
prove z3
show new_proof /unknown
exit
